        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119">

                <pb facs="0287" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg163"/>

                <head>No. 119.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Martinez to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Chili in the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1881-10-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 27, 1881</date>. (Received November 1.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 28.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the pleasure to inform your
                    excellency that the treaty for the settlement of the boundary question,
                    concluded between Chili and the Argentine Republic, having been approved by the
                    Congresses of both nations, has been ratified, and that the ratifications have
                    been exchanged.</p>
                <p>As very valuable services were lent in the conclusion of that treaty by the
                    honorable ministers of the United States at Santiago and Buenos Ayres, my
                    government through me, performs the pleasing duty of returning its warmest
                    thanks to your excellency, as it has already done personally to the
                    distinguished diplomatist Thomas H. [meaning A.] Osborn.</p>
                <p>With sentiments, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>M. MARTINEZ.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
